The issue's main idea, using overlapped segments trimmed to the speaker's own turns, was not built: on the sample video the guest's only speech outside their one line is ~2 s of backchannels, all over the host's voice, and cutting audio inside overlapped speech leaves a transcript that no longer matches the clip, which is exactly what makes F5 speak reference words before every line (#5). So the automatic improvement is limited to adding sub-1 s lines, and only when the reference would otherwise stay under MIN_REFERENCE (5 s), because short lines are lower quality than longer ones but better than a too-short reference. The manual override is the real fix for such speakers. A manual .txt transcript is assumed to be in the video's language, since without a language F5's reference text is not romanized for Japanese and the reference leaks; a clip without .txt takes Whisper's detected language instead. VOICE_REFERENCE_FILES (file ids of the folder's .wav/.txt files) is derived in main and fingerprinted, for the same reason as GLOSSARY in #31: a folder path alone would not re-run the stage when a clip is replaced.
